#---
# purpose: "A forwarded closure that carries captures reaches its own body with its own capture record"
# oracle: oracle.exs
#---
#
# fz-kdt.125, the capture half. `run/2` forwards its callable to `apply_twice/2`,
# which invokes it and therefore specializes on the closure literal: two bodies,
# each grounded on its own lambda. `run/2`'s single callsite names both.
#
# Both lambdas capture one integer, so the two specializations of `apply_twice/2`
# want that capture as a lane while `run/2` holds the callable boxed. The routing
# and the ABI are both at stake: the plan has to name which lambda arrived, and
# the caller has to hand that lambda's own capture record to the body it routes
# to. `12` is `n + 1` twice over `10`; `210` is `n + 100` twice over `10`.
defmodule Pipeline do
  fn apply_twice(f, x), do: f.(f.(x))
  fn run(f, x), do: apply_twice(f, x)
end

fn main() do
  a = 1
  b = 100
  dbg(Pipeline.run(fn (n) -> n + a end, 10))
  dbg(Pipeline.run(fn (n) -> n + b end, 10))
end
